.TH "EPX\-AI" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-ai \- read and change AI agents and their setup, chat with them, generate texts
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai [flags]
epx ai [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads the AI Service\(aqs agents and what they are built from: agent templates, tools, tokens, OAuth configurations and MCP servers, the LLM models of the supported providers and the commerce events that can trigger an agent; what agents did: their jobs, conversations, request and session logs and analytics; and which fields the AI RAG Indexer embeds. Upserts, changes and deletes agents and what they are built from, exports and imports agents, chats with them and generates texts, which consumes AI credits. \fBepx ai rag reindex\fR embeds the entities of a type again.
.PP
Its reads require the ai.agent_read scope. Its writes require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx ai agents"
Read, create, upsert, change, delete, export and import AI agents.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents [flags]
epx ai agents [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads AI agents: TYPE is generic, complaint or anti_fraud, PROVIDER and MODEL the LLM an agent uses and TRIGGERS what starts it (endpoint, slack, teams or commerce_events). Their prompts, tools and MCP servers are only in \fB\-o json\fR.
.PP
Its reads require the ai.agent_read scope. Its writes require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them.
.SS "epx ai agents attach"
Attach a file to a chat with an agent.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents attach AGENT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Uploads the file that \fB\-\-upload\fR names (jpg, jpeg, png, pdf, csv, text or txt), or assigns the media asset that \fB\-\-media\fR names (\fBepx media list\fR), to the agent AGENT_ID, the ID that \fBepx ai agents list\fR shows, in the session that \fB\-\-session\fR names, or a new one. Emporix answers with the attachment\(aqs id and the sessionId, which \fBepx ai chat\fR with that agent takes as \fB\-\-attachment\fR and \fB\-\-session\fR.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the ai.agentexecution_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-media <ID>\fR
The ID of a media asset to attach.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-session <ID>\fR
The ID of the session to go on with, the sessionId of an earlier chat or attachment; without it, a new one.
.TP
\fB\-\-upload <PATH>\fR
The file in PATH to upload (up to 30 MB including the form), sent with its name.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents attach complaint\-agent \-\-upload order.pdf \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx ai agents create"
Create an agent from a template.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents create TEMPLATE_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates an agent from the agent template TEMPLATE_ID, the ID that \fBepx ai templates list\fR shows, which must be enabled, with the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR: its name and description, its userPrompt and, optionally, its id. Emporix answers with the id of the agent.
.PP
Localized text in the body, such as a name, is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "gram", "de": "Gramm"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, or with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR LANGUAGE a string in that language, e.g. \fB"gram"\fR with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR en.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-content\-language <LANGUAGE>\fR
The LANGUAGE of localized text in the body, or * for maps of translations. Default: \fB*\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents create complaint\-template \-\-file agent.json \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx ai agents delete"
Delete an agent.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the agent ID. Emporix refuses to delete one that others use, unless \fB\-\-force\fR unassigns it from them. ID is the ID that \fBepx ai agents list\fR shows.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Delete it even where other agents collaborate with it.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx ai agents export"
Export agents, which creates an export job.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents export [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Exports the agents that \fB\-\-agent\fR names (up to 100) with the tools and MCP servers they use, and prints the export: data, the agents base64\-encoded, and its checksum, which \fBepx ai agents import\fR takes on another tenant. Emporix keeps each export as a job of type EXPORT, the jobId of the response, which \fBepx ai jobs get JOB_ID\fR reads. It changes data although Emporix needs no write\-capable scope for it.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-agent <ID>\fR
The ID of an agent to export (repeatable; required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents export \-\-agent complaint\-agent \-\-yes > agents.json
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx ai agents get"
Show one agent.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads AI agents: TYPE is generic, complaint or anti_fraud, PROVIDER and MODEL the LLM an agent uses and TRIGGERS what starts it (endpoint, slack, teams or commerce_events). Their prompts, tools and MCP servers are only in \fB\-o json\fR.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, ENABLED, PROVIDER, MODEL, TRIGGERS, NAME.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx ai agents import"
Import agents.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents import [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Imports the agents of an export, with the tools and MCP servers they use, from the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR: the data and checksum that \fBepx ai agents export\fR prints, which Emporix checks. Imported agents start disabled; Emporix answers with what it imported and the jobId of the IMPORT job that it keeps (\fBepx ai jobs get JOB_ID\fR).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents import \-\-file agents.json \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx ai agents list"
List AI agents.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads AI agents: TYPE is generic, complaint or anti_fraud, PROVIDER and MODEL the LLM an agent uses and TRIGGERS what starts it (endpoint, slack, teams or commerce_events). Their prompts, tools and MCP servers are only in \fB\-o json\fR.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, ENABLED, PROVIDER, MODEL, TRIGGERS, NAME.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx ai agents patch"
Change members of an agent.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents patch ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Changes the agent ID with the JSON array of operations in \fB\-\-file\fR, each with op (ADD, REMOVE or REPLACE), path and value, e.g. \fB[{"op": "REPLACE", "path": "/enabled", "value": false}]\fR; its other members keep their values. ID is the ID that \fBepx ai agents list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PATCH. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx ai agents search"
Search AI agents.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents search [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the AI agents that an Emporix q filter finds (\fB\-\-query\fR; without it, every one). It reads and shows them as \fBepx ai agents list\fR does.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, ENABLED, PROVIDER, MODEL, TRIGGERS, NAME.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, sent as given in the request body, not in the URL (empty: no filter), e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx ai agents update"
Upsert an agent.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai agents update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the agent ID with the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR, or creates it with that ID where none exists (an upsert): Emporix answers with the id of one it created and nothing for one it replaced. With metadata.version, as \fBepx ai agents get ID \-o json\fR prints it, Emporix replaces only that version: another is a conflict (exit 5). The JSON holds its name and description, userPrompt, llmConfig, triggers and mcpServers, and its nativeTools, agentCollaborations, enabledMemory and maxRecursionLimit. ID is the ID that \fBepx ai agents list\fR shows.
.PP
Localized text in the body, such as a name, is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "gram", "de": "Gramm"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, or with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR LANGUAGE a string in that language, e.g. \fB"gram"\fR with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR en.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-content\-language <LANGUAGE>\fR
The LANGUAGE of localized text in the body, or * for maps of translations. Default: \fB*\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx ai analytics"
Read the analytics of agents.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai analytics [flags]
epx ai analytics [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads what Emporix counts of the requests and sessions of agents, as its dashboards show them.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_read scope.
.SS "epx ai analytics agent"
Show the request and session totals of one agent.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai analytics agent AGENT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the totals of the requests and sessions of one agent: AGENT_ID is the ID that \fBepx ai agents list\fR shows; an unknown one counts nothing. LOGS is requests or sessions, TOTAL how many there were in the last four weeks, WARNING and ERROR how many of them had that severity and ERROR RATE their share with errors, as Emporix computes it. The requests per session and the weekly trends are only in \fB\-o json\fR.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among LOGS, TOTAL, WARNING, ERROR, ERROR RATE.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx ai analytics executions"
List how often agents ran per calendar quarter, month or week.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai analytics executions AGENT_IDS [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads how often agents ran (their sessions) per calendar quarter, Emporix\(aqs default granularity, or per month or week (\fB\-\-granularity\fR): each PERIOD that Emporix reports runs from FROM (inclusive) to TO (exclusive), in UTC. AGENT_IDS are the IDs that \fBepx ai agents list\fR shows, separated by commas without spaces (at most 100); an unknown one ran 0 times.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among AGENT, PERIOD, FROM, TO, EXECUTIONS.
.TP
\fB\-\-granularity <period>\fR
The calendar period of each count: QUARTER, MONTH or WEEK.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx ai analytics tenant"
Show the request and session totals of every agent.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai analytics tenant [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the totals of the requests and sessions of every agent of the tenant. LOGS is requests or sessions, TOTAL how many there were in the last four weeks, WARNING and ERROR how many of them had that severity and ERROR RATE their share with errors, as Emporix computes it. The requests per session and the weekly trends are only in \fB\-o json\fR.
.PP
Requires the ai.agent_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among LOGS, TOTAL, WARNING, ERROR, ERROR RATE.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx ai chat"
Send a message to an agent and print its reply (consumes AI credits).
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai chat [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sends the message that \fB\-\-message\fR gives to the agent \fB\-\-agent\fR, and prints its reply: the messages of the agent and of those it collaborates with, each with the sessionId that \fB\-\-session\fR takes to go on. A reply may take longer than the \fB\-\-timeout\fR of a request (30s by default): then give a longer one, e.g. \fB\-\-timeout\fR 5m, or use chat\-async. It consumes AI credits: the LLM tokens of the agent\(aqs model, and of the agents it collaborates with. With \fB\-\-session\fR, the chat goes on in that session, which the agent remembers where its enabledMemory is true; an attachment must be one of the session, attached to the same agent (\fBepx ai agents attach\fR). \fB\-\-file\fR gives the body instead, with the caption and purpose of each attachment.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the ai.agentexecution_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-agent <ID>\fR
The ID of the agent, as \fBepx ai agents list\fR shows it (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-attachment <ID>\fR
The ID of an attachment of the session to send with the message, as \fBepx ai agents attach\fR prints it (repeatable) (only with \fB\-\-session\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-message <TEXT>\fR
The TEXT to send to the agent (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-session <ID>\fR
The ID of the session to go on with, the sessionId of an earlier chat or attachment; without it, a new one.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai chat \-\-agent complaint\-agent \-\-message "Find order EON1243" \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx ai chat\-async"
Send a message to an agent, which replies in a job (consumes AI credits).
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai chat\-async [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sends the message that \fB\-\-message\fR gives to the agent \fB\-\-agent\fR, which replies in a job of type AGENT_CHAT: Emporix answers with its jobId, which \fBepx ai jobs get JOB_ID\fR reads. It consumes AI credits: the LLM tokens of the agent\(aqs model, and of the agents it collaborates with. With \fB\-\-session\fR, the chat goes on in that session, which the agent remembers where its enabledMemory is true; an attachment must be one of the session, attached to the same agent (\fBepx ai agents attach\fR). \fB\-\-file\fR gives the body instead, with the caption and purpose of each attachment.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the ai.agentexecution_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-agent <ID>\fR
The ID of the agent, as \fBepx ai agents list\fR shows it (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-attachment <ID>\fR
The ID of an attachment of the session to send with the message, as \fBepx ai agents attach\fR prints it (repeatable) (only with \fB\-\-session\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
