.SS "epx ai generate\-completion"
Generate the next message of a chat history (consumes AI credits).
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai generate\-completion [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generates the next message of the chat history that \fB\-\-message\fR gives, one message per \fB\-\-message\fR in their order, and prints it as result. It consumes AI credits: the LLM tokens of the tenant\(aqs own OpenAI account where the tenant configuration openAiApiToken holds its token, or else Emporix\(aqs, of which a tenant may use 3 million input and 1 million output tokens. A reply may take longer than the \fB\-\-timeout\fR of a request (30s by default): then give a longer one, e.g. \fB\-\-timeout\fR 5m.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the ai.completion_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-message <ROLE:TEXT>\fR
A message of the chat history as ROLE:TEXT, ROLE SYSTEM, USER or ASSISTANT (repeatable; required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx ai generate\-completion \-\-message "SYSTEM:You write product texts" \e
  \-\-message "USER:Describe product 100200"
.fi
.RE
