.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Disable it even where enabled agents use it, which disables them too.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBepx\fR(1) for the global options, the credentials epx reads and its exit codes; https://commerce-cloud-integrations.github.io/emporix-cli/commands/ai
